	<entry>
		<id>https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/w-h-davies/the-autobiography-of-a-super-tramp</id>
		<dc:identifier>https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/w-h-davies/the-autobiography-of-a-super-tramp</dc:identifier>
		<title>The Autobiography of a Super-Tramp</title>
		<author>
			<name>W. H. Davies</name>
			<uri>https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/w-h-davies</uri>
			<schema:alternateName>William Henry Davies</schema:alternateName>
			<schema:sameAs>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/W._H._Davies</schema:sameAs>
			<schema:sameAs>https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n83139060.html</schema:sameAs>
		</author>
		<published>2026-09-22T15:40:20Z</published>
		<dc:issued>2026-09-22T15:40:20Z</dc:issued>
		<updated>2026-09-22T15:40:21Z</updated>
		<dc:language>en-GB</dc:language>
		<dc:publisher>Standard Ebooks</dc:publisher>
		<rights>Public domain in the United States. Users located outside of the United States must check their local laws before using this ebook. Original content released to the public domain via the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication.</rights>
		<summary type="text">At the end of the 19th century, a destitute tramp wanders across England and North America.</summary>
		<content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;The Autobiography of a Super-Tramp&lt;/i&gt;, poet &lt;a href="https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/w-h-davies"&gt;W. H. Davies’&lt;/a&gt; autobiography, recalls spurning a youth of subsistence and squalor in England to pursue a life of travel abroad. With quiet and understated prose, Davies recounts a tramp’s life: riding railroad boxcars and evading fare collectors, cadging free meals, working as a migrant field hand, and dealing with corrupt law enforcement and judges. Each encounter gives Davies a chance to share his observations on the state of America and England at the turn of the 20th century.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Davies’ anti-authoritarianism inspired contemporaries like George Bernard Shaw—who both lobbied for the book’s publication and provided its preface—as well as future drifters like Christopher “Alexander Supertramp” McCandless.&lt;/p&gt;</content>
		<category scheme="http://purl.org/dc/terms/LCSH" term="Poets, English--20th century--Biography"/>
		<category scheme="http://purl.org/dc/terms/LCSH" term="Davies, W. H. (William Henry), 1871-1940"/>
		<category scheme="http://purl.org/dc/terms/LCSH" term="Tramps--Biography"/>
		<category scheme="https://standardebooks.org/vocab/subjects" term="Autobiography"/>
		<category scheme="https://standardebooks.org/vocab/subjects" term="Travel"/>
		<link href="https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/w-h-davies/the-autobiography-of-a-super-tramp/downloads/cover.jpg" rel="http://opds-spec.org/image" type="image/jpeg"/>
