	</entry>
	<entry>
		<id>https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/edmund-burke/reflections-on-the-revolution-in-france</id>
		<dc:identifier>https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/edmund-burke/reflections-on-the-revolution-in-france</dc:identifier>
		<title>Reflections on the Revolution in France</title>
		<author>
			<name>Edmund Burke</name>
			<uri>https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/edmund-burke</uri>
			<schema:sameAs>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edmund_Burke</schema:sameAs>
			<schema:sameAs>https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n79040055.html</schema:sameAs>
		</author>
		<published>2026-09-11T15:04:18Z</published>
		<dc:issued>2026-09-11T15:04:18Z</dc:issued>
		<updated>2026-09-11T15:04:21Z</updated>
		<dc:language>en-US</dc:language>
		<dc:publisher>Standard Ebooks</dc:publisher>
		<rights>Public domain in the United States. Users located outside of the United States must check their local laws before using this ebook. Original content released to the public domain via the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication.</rights>
		<summary type="text">The conservative political theorist Edmund Burke critiques the political program of the French Revolution.</summary>
		<content type="html">&lt;p&gt;Written in 1790 during the early stages of the French Revolution, &lt;i&gt;Reflections on the Revolution in France&lt;/i&gt; is regarded as one of the foundational texts of conservative political theory. In it, the British philosopher and statesman &lt;a href="https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/edmund-burke"&gt;Edmund Burke&lt;/a&gt; critiques the political program of the French Revolution, dismissing it as a political order founded on abstract principles. Instead, Burke advocates for constitutional rule based on received institutions, incremental reform, and sensitivity to the vagaries of human nature. Some of Burke’s predictions, such as the revolutionary government becoming a “mischievous and ignoble oligarchy” and the politicization of the military bringing about a “military republic,” proved to be prescient in the face of the Reign of Terror and Napoleon’s coup of 18 Brumaire.&lt;/p&gt;</content>
		<category scheme="http://purl.org/dc/terms/LCSH" term="Great Britain--Politics and government--1760-1820"/>
		<category scheme="http://purl.org/dc/terms/LCSH" term="Political science--Early works to 1800"/>
		<category scheme="https://standardebooks.org/vocab/subjects" term="Nonfiction"/>
		<category scheme="https://standardebooks.org/vocab/subjects" term="Philosophy"/>
		<link href="https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/edmund-burke/reflections-on-the-revolution-in-france/downloads/cover.jpg" rel="http://opds-spec.org/image" type="image/jpeg"/>
		<link href="https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/edmund-burke/reflections-on-the-revolution-in-france/downloads/cover-thumbnail.jpg" rel="http://opds-spec.org/image/thumbnail" type="image/jpeg"/>
		<link href="https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/edmund-burke/reflections-on-the-revolution-in-france" rel="alternate" title="This ebook’s page at Standard Ebooks" type="application/xhtml+xml"/>
