	<entry>
		<id>https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/theodore-roosevelt/a-book-lovers-holidays-in-the-open</id>
		<dc:identifier>https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/theodore-roosevelt/a-book-lovers-holidays-in-the-open</dc:identifier>
		<title>A Book-Lover’s Holidays in the Open</title>
		<author>
			<name>Theodore Roosevelt</name>
			<uri>https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/theodore-roosevelt</uri>
			<schema:alternateName>Theodore Roosevelt Jr.</schema:alternateName>
			<schema:sameAs>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_Roosevelt</schema:sameAs>
			<schema:sameAs>https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n79027239.html</schema:sameAs>
		</author>
		<published>2026-09-04T20:20:13Z</published>
		<dc:issued>2026-09-04T20:20:13Z</dc:issued>
		<updated>2026-09-04T20:38:48Z</updated>
		<dc:language>en-US</dc:language>
		<dc:publisher>Standard Ebooks</dc:publisher>
		<rights>Public domain in the United States. Users located outside of the United States must check their local laws before using this ebook. Original content released to the public domain via the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication.</rights>
		<summary type="text">Outdoorsman and former U.S. president Theodore Roosevelt weaves his love of reading into the stories of his travels through the Americas.</summary>
		<content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;A Book-Lover’s Holidays in the Open&lt;/i&gt; is a travelogue written by former U.S. president &lt;a href="https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/theodore-roosevelt"&gt;Theodore Roosevelt&lt;/a&gt; about his expeditions through the Americas following his presidency in the early twentieth century. In it, Roosevelt takes readers on a cougar hunt in the Grand Canyon, through the Andes and Northern Patagonia, to a Mississippi River bird reserve, and to a Hopi snake dance, among other exotic and beautiful locations.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Roosevelt blends his love for reading and literature with these adventures, giving readers a glimpse into the books he would have brought on his outdoor journeys.&lt;/p&gt;</content>
